# SRG-APP-000815-AU-000260  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must require users to be individually authenticated
# before granting access to the shared accounts or resources.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000815-AU-000260
group:           V-263572
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-004045
control_rev5:    IA-2

contribution:    Splunk authenticates every session against the authentication system named
                 in authentication.conf [authentication] authType and has no anonymous or
                 guest mode to disable, so access to shared resources is always preceded by
                 an individual authentication; shared access is then delivered by role
                 membership and role inheritance (authorize.conf [role_<roleName>]
                 importRoles) rather than by a shared login. The condition below therefore
                 confirms an authentication system is in force - it cannot tell one person
                 from several people using one account.

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.

check:           authentication.conf [authentication] authType non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          authentication.conf [authentication] authType https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Issuance of an individual account per person and the prohibition on shared
                 credentials - carried by organizational account management; no product
                 setting can distinguish two people sharing one credential.
external:        Where authType is LDAP, SAML, or ProxySSO, the individual authentication
                 event occurs at the directory service or identity provider.
external:        The built-in admin account retained as the account of last resort -
                 carried by the documented break-glass procedure; the product STIG's own
                 check text assumes no other local accounts exist.
external:        Whether a role shared through authorize.conf importRoles grants more than
                 a person's duties require - an organizational access-control
                 determination.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:26 ([authentication]), :30
                 (authType = [Splunk|LDAP|Scripted|SAML|ProxySSO], default Splunk);
                 splunk-spec-files/authorize.conf.spec:67 ([role_<roleName>]), :79
                 (importRoles)
finding:         No authentication system is in force for the instance (authentication.conf
                 [authentication] authType is empty), so access to shared roles and
                 knowledge objects is not preceded by an individual authentication; this
                 determination is from the perspective of the application layer alone, the
                 uniqueness of each account being an account-management matter outside the
                 application.
